  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-RAD-05 and RBC-LAB-03. 12 of 13 items closed; 1 left open on purpose.\n\nOriginal items:\n- pt-0006 Patel, CT urogram (task-00001): no cause found for the hematuria. The incidental 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening, so the annual LDCT was ordered (sr-t0001), with tracking task, message and note. Superseded later (see below).\n- pt-0016 Ondricka, TSH (task-00010): normal, closed. Potassium (task-00011): corrected from 6.3 to 4.4, normal, closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, preliminary CTA (task-00003): acted on the final report dr-00084. No PE; the \"nodule\" is a vessel; no follow-up needed. Closed.\n- pt-0007 BMP (task-00004): creatinine 1.64 vs 0.98 about 35 h earlier, which is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0009), patient messaged, note. PRN naproxen left active and flagged for your review.\n- pt-0064 Marchetti, ED BMP 9/26 (task-64001): creatinine 1.36 with no earlier result in the comparison window, so not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0033 Whitfield, BMP (task-00025): creatinine 1.31. The 0.84 marked entered in error was excluded; not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Brennan, K 6.4 (task-00005): first handled as hemolyzed (urgent repeat sr-t0015, message, note). Changed after the correction below.\n\nArrived while I worked:\n- pt-0008 correction (inbox-a0005): the specimen was not hemolyzed and K 6.4 stands. Switched to the critical pathway: STAT message to pool-oncall, stat BMP today (sr-t0019), corrected message asking him to come in today, addendum note. Med review: no potassium-raising drug to hold (metoprolol kept for IHD).\n- pt-0033 creatinine 1.78 from urgent care (inbox-a0004): up 0.47 from 1.31 nine hours earlier, which is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0024), patient messaged, note.\n- pt-0064 creatinine 1.48 (inbox-a0003): no earlier result in the window, so not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0006 outside addendum to the 4/14/26 screening LDCT (inbox-a0001): new 5 mm RUL nodule, Lung-RADS 3, LDCT in 6 months. Ordered LDCT for 10/23–11/14/26 (sr-t0029), tracking task due 11/14, corrected message, note.\n\nLeft open:\n- inbox-a0002, pt-0007 chest X-ray: preliminary read only (possible 7 mm RUL opacity). No final report yet, so it stays open per §2(c).\n\nNeeds you:\n- I couldn't cancel orders or my own tasks here. Please discontinue the 2027 LDCT order sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002; task-t0031 asks you to.\n- sr-t0015 (pt-0008's urgent repeat BMP) is still active. The stat BMP replaces it, and I recorded that in the chart. Please discontinue it too, since no task asks for that.\n\nAlso noted, not acted on:\n- pt-0006 has a hemolyzed BMP from 10/21 (dr-00071) that is not in your inbox.\n- pt-0006's smoking status conflicts: the H&P says current smoker, the structured record says ex-smoker. It doesn't change the plan.\n- Six refill messages in your messages queue were already there when I started and are untouched.",
